From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Proton GE Team <proton-ge@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:15:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Clamp negative video source timestamps to zero.

Progressive MP4 streams may begin with a negative video presentation
timestamp because of encoder delay and B-frame reordering. Media Foundation
source readers expose a presentation timeline beginning at zero, and some
consumers seek back to zero or reject the stream when Wine exposes that
negative first sample directly.

Clamp only the presentation timestamp of compressed video samples. Keep the
decode timestamp untouched because a negative DTS remains meaningful for
decoder ordering.
---
 dlls/winedmo/media_source.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -1080,7 +1080,8 @@ static HRESULT media_stream_send_sample(struct media_stream *stream, struct medi
     if (stream->is_video && pkt->dts != INT64_MIN)
         IMFSample_SetUINT64(sample, &MFSampleExtension_DecodeTimestamp, pkt->dts);
     if (pkt->pts != INT64_MIN)
-        IMFSample_SetSampleTime(sample, pkt->pts);
+        IMFSample_SetSampleTime(sample,
+                stream->is_video && pkt->pts < 0 ? 0 : pkt->pts);
     if (pkt->duration != INT64_MIN)
         IMFSample_SetSampleDuration(sample, pkt->duration);
     if (token)
